    {
      "title": "The serial port re-enumerates",
      "text": "Because USB is handled by the sketch's own chip, the COM port disappears on reset and during upload; `while (!Serial)` waits for the monitor to connect.",
      "source": "arduino-docs"
    },
    {
      "title": "I2C moved to D2/D3",
      "text": "SDA and SCL are on D2 and D3 (and the R3 header pins), not A4/A5 as on the Uno.",
      "source": "arduino-docs"
    },
    {
      "title": "5 V logic",
      "text": "I/O is 5 V. Sensors and modules that run at 3.3 V (most modern ones) need level shifting on their inputs.",
